that starts `Each row carries` to contain each name wrapped in backticks. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the first name. Then in `CBR` replace the sentence `Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill.` with ``Each row carries `command`, the runnable slash command, `policy`, its derived policy, `mutating`, the class that says what a run writes (`read-only`, `add-only` or `mutates`) when the record names one, and `ownerSkillId`, the owning skill.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c \"its derived policy and the owning skill\" $CBR` prints nothing.\n87: - [ ] T009 [P] Escape line breaks in generated string literals (`DER`, `DCS`). Test first: create `DCS` with the module banner the other test files use and a comment saying a generated literal holding a raw line break no longer parses, so the generated source would stop compiling. Load `DER` with `createRequire(import.meta.url)` as `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` does, and add `it.each([['LF', 'a\\nb'], ['CR', 'a\\rb'], ['U+2028', 'a\\u2028b'], ['U+2029', 'a\\u2029b'], ['a quote and a backslash', \"it's a \\\\ path\"]])('round-trips a value holding %s', (_label, value) => ...)`, expecting `tsString(value)` to match `/^'[^\\n\\r\\u2028\\u2029]*'$/` and `new Function('return ' + tsString(value) + ';')()` to equal `value`. Run `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` and see it fail because `tsString` is not exported. Then in `DER` add `tsString` to `module.exports`, and in `tsString` chain `.replaceAll('\\n', '\\\\n').replaceAll('\\r', '\\\\r').replaceAll('\\u2028', '\\\\u2028').replaceAll('\\u2029', '\\\\u2029')` after the two existing `replaceAll` calls. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `node $PL/pr